## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical cache invalidation and per-tenant isolation with Redis. It emphasizes correctness over theory and keeps memory footprints predictable.

## Key Concepts
- Cache-aside pattern with tenant keys
- TTL tuning and avoidance of stampedes
- Pub/Sub vs. central bus for invalidation

## Code Example
```javascript
const KEY = (tid, pid) => `tenant:${tid}:product:${pid}`
async function getWithCache(tid, pid, loadFromDb, cache, ttl=300){
  const k = KEY(tid, pid)
  let v = await cache.get(k)
  if (v) return JSON.parse(v)
  const row = await loadFromDb(tid, pid)
  await cache.set(k, JSON.stringify(row), ttl)
  return row
}
// on update
async function invalidate(tid, pid, pub, cache){
  await pub.publish(`tenant:${tid}:cache:product`, JSON.stringify({pid}))
  await cache.del(KEY(tid,pid))
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle cross-tenant eviction storms if many tenants update simultaneously?
- How would you monitor cache hit rate and TTL effectiveness in production?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates cache invalidation strategies at scale, per-tenant data isolation, and stampede protection mechanisms in Redis-based systems. It also tests understanding of Pub/Sub invalidation patterns and lightweight locking approaches.

## Key Concepts

- Write-through cache architecture
- Per-tenant TTL management and version stamping
- Distributed locking to prevent cache stampede
- Pub/Sub-based invalidation and out-of-band refresh
- Performance trade-offs: data freshness vs. system load

## Code Example

```javascript
async function getProduct(id, tenant) {
  const cacheKey = `prod:${tenant}:${id}`;
  let data = await redis.get(cacheKey);
  if (data) return JSON.parse(data);

  const lockKey = `${cacheKey}:lock`;
  const lock = await redis.set(lockKey, '1', 'PX', 5000, 'NX');

  if (lock) {
    try {
      const freshData = await fetchFromDB(id, tenant);
      await redis.setex(cacheKey, 300, JSON.stringify(freshData));
      return freshData;
    } finally {
      await redis.del(lockKey);
    }
  }

  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));
  return getProduct(id, tenant);
}
```

